WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
- You obviously don't take
this job very seriously.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:02.520
- I do, sir.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.290
It's just these particular marbles.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.050
I just needed to feel what
they felt like in my mouth.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.570
I don't know what is wrong with me.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.400
- You know we do serious
business here, right?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.360
- Yes, I do know that.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.920
I'm 100% aware of that. Yep.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.477
- 'Cause I've forgotten where I was!

00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:18.150
- You were saying that Justice
is a dumb blind old lady.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.202
I heard every word.
- Yes.

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:20.035
No!

00:00:20.035 --> 00:00:22.113
She's not dumb.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.130
But she is blind.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.900
She's reminiscent of

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.040
Kerry Washington.
(dramatic music)

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.282
You know?

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:33.032
(dramatic music)

00:00:34.173 --> 00:00:36.940
(percussive music)

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.820
- Okay. Alright.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.320
Good morning, Tom.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.970
Jason.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.110
How ya doing there, Dave?

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.190
Crystal.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.210
Tommy.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.590
Good morning, Jake.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.000
How are ya?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.550
- Pretty good, Kenny.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.840
You know, it's so early in the morning.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.990
I'm sorry to be the
bearer of bad news, but...

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.420
You know how I was supposed
to work late tonight?

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.253
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:58.253 --> 00:00:59.250
- Well, I gotta run this errand

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.450
for Mr. Mahina,

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.340
and he says that you're
gonna have to cover for me.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.180
So there it is.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.188
I don't even... I'm sorry.

00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:05.533
(Kenny whistles)
Drop the ax.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:06.366
(Kenny laughs)

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.380
Okay. So...

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.403
- Hmm.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.410
Again?

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.243
- Yeah.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.890
Oh, you know what?

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.360
Just remembered.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.460
Mr. Mahina also -

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.293
almost slipped my mind -

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:20.760
wants us to change parking spaces.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.593
- What?!

00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:22.426
- Yeah.

00:01:22.426 --> 00:01:23.259
Me, personally,

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:25.140
I enjoy the nine-minute walk,

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.180
but he said that we have to do it.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.460
Believe it, I hate it as much as you do.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.360
- What are you gonna do?

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.350
- Nothing you can do.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.302
- Mr. Mahina said it.

00:01:32.302 --> 00:01:33.840
- Mahina.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.790
This whole situation
has been Mahina-nized.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.040
- It just seems a little confusing to me

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.490
as to why Mr. Mahina would give a (bleep)

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.320
where we park.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.160
- How's that?

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.030
- I mean, why would he care where we park?

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.530
- I don't know the
answer to that question.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:50.491
I mean, that's... It's just what he said.

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:53.220
He... Hey, the Mahina
works in mysterious ways.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.053
- You know what?

00:01:54.053 --> 00:01:55.080
I'm gonna ask him myself, 'cause...

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:55.950
- No! That's okay!

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.783
I'll do it!

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.846
(door opening)

00:02:01.846 --> 00:02:03.900
(door closing)

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.490
Mr. Mahina, sir, I know you're busy,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:08.160
but can I speak to you
about the parking switch?

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.018
- ["Mr. Mahina"] What is
there to talk about, Kenny?

00:02:10.018 --> 00:02:13.127
I told you and Jake to
switch parking spaces.

00:02:13.127 --> 00:02:14.786
Don't you know who I am?

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:16.378
I am Mr. Mahina

00:02:16.378 --> 00:02:19.498
and I'm a real, real person in here.

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:22.581
Now you get the hell outta my office.

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:26.357
- Wow.

00:02:26.357 --> 00:02:27.840
Did you hear that? It was crazy in there.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.250
I mean, that was

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.083
whew!

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:30.916
tense.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:31.770
- Yeah.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.680
You know what's really crazy, though?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.720
I've been working here for about a year

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.240
and I've never even seen Mr. Mahina.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.170
- Well, see, now, that's,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.100
that's an easy one to answer.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.000
That's because he comes in

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:42.960
before you come into work

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.160
and he's still working when you leave.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.540
That's what makes him
Mr. Mahina, you know?

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.373
Come on.

00:02:46.373 --> 00:02:47.818
We're talking about
Mr. Mahina here, right?

00:02:47.818 --> 00:02:48.651
(both laugh)

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:49.860
- It makes perfect sense.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.690
You know, I bet
- Mm-hmm?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.070
